  "title": "Ukraine's Pro-Kremlin Party Wins Election Amid War Reach",
  "summary": "Ukraine's pro-Kremlin party won a landslide victory in the State Duma election, with 49 deputies elected from war veterans, as Russia's military and political landscape intensifies. The results highlight the growing war's impact on Moscow and Russia's position in the conflict.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Ukraine's pro-Kremlin party won a record 355 seats in the country’s 450-seat Duma lower house of parliament, according to preliminary figures.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Russia’s new parliament will include 49 deputies who have taken part in the war against Ukraine, officials have said after a landslide victory by the ruling United Russia party.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Ukraine launched over 1,000 drones at Russia during the State Duma election’s final day, including hundreds targeting Moscow.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
